class_name Moves
extends RefCounted
## Move data: timings, damage, cost and what the opponent can do about it.
## Each move's behavior lives in scripts/moves/ ("script"). Every balance number is here.
##   power, pp, accuracy, priority the games' numbers (Showdown). Damage comes from power with
##                                 the games' formula (see Damage); cooldown from PP and power
##                                 (cooldown() below). accuracy 0 = never misses
##   split                         how many of our hits make one use in the games: both Dragon
##                                 Claw swipes deal what one use deals there; each hit, its
##                                 share. Streams count about half their ticks (Flamethrower 8
##                                 of 15, Hydro Pump 6 of 10): nobody lands them all, so a well
##                                 aimed stream reaches one use and holding it on longer, more
##   power_by                      power not fixed in the games: "speed" (Electro Ball), "status"
##                                 (Facade), "lowered" (Lash Out: double while Fighter.lowered_t runs)
##   crit                          always a critical hit (Damage.CRIT): ignores the user's lowered
##                                 attack and the target's raised defense
##   needs_attacking               only connects while the target winds up or runs a move that
##                                 deals damage; otherwise "But it failed!" (Sucker Punch)
##   protects                      a guard that contact moves with Unseen Fist go through
##   hits_def                      special, but measured against the target's Defense (Psyshock)
##   disables                      seconds every move of the target not already cooling down has
##                                 to wait (Disable, Fighter._disable_all)
##   boosts                        stat -> stages it gains at the end of a self boost (selfboost.gd)
##   off_edge                      it can carry the user off a stage's edge (Teleport); no other
##                                 move does (Fighter._edge_stop)
##   power_at                      the "damage" value that equals one use in the games (Aura
##                                 Sphere: uncharged below it, fully charged above)
##   startup / active / recovery   seconds of wind-up, active phase and recovery
##   cost / cd                     energy, and cooldown for moves without power (status
##                                 moves keep their designed one)
##   damage, lift (m/s upward), stun (s), knocks_down, hitstop (impact pause). With power,
##                                 "damage" only sets each hit's share (see power_at)
##   knock                         meters it slides the target (push moves); without it, from
##                                 strength (see Knockback: 0.3 / 1 / 2.5 m)
##   strength                      0 light, 1 medium, 2 heavy (sound, rumble, effects)
##   poise                         while it winds up and runs, only hits with
##                                 strength >= move poise + Pokémon poise interrupt it
##                                 (0 by default: any hit from a light Pokémon cuts it)
##   needs_ground                  used in the air, the Pokémon dives and does it on landing
##   manual_aim                    continuous multi-hit streams (Hydro Pump, Flamethrower): the
##                                 player turns with the stick, no horizontal assist; the rival's
##                                 height is aimed automatically. manual_turn: how fast it turns.
##                                 Discrete attacks (single-hit beams, projectiles) aim themselves
##   cancels_dodge                 its recovery can be cancelled with a dodge
##   cancels_into_moves            if it lands, its recovery can be cancelled into another move
##   deflects                      its hit stops projectiles: 1 breaks them, 2 sends them back
##                                 (Combat.deflect); deflectable on a projectile: how far it can
##                                 be deflected (2 by default, 1 only breaks)
##   inflicts                      status moves: the status they give ("drowsy": Yawn)
##   secondary                     what a hit also does, as in the games: "chance", and "status",
##                                 "boost" or "confuse" (seconds) on the target, "self" on the user
##   heal                          share of the damage dealt the user gets back at the hit
##                                 (Draining Kiss, Fighter.on_strike)
##   stars, fan, gap               Swift: how many, how wide they leave (rad to each side) and the
##                                 seconds between them
##   look                          which wave widewave.gd draws: "gleam" or "voice"
##   counterplay                   what the opponent can do (for design and the selection screen)
## Player-facing text (display_name, desc, counterplay) is in English and is translated
## through game/i18n/translations.csv.

## The type a move has in battle: Pixilate turns Normal moves into Fairy ones.
static func type_for(id: String, ability: String) -> String:
	var type: String = DATA[id].type if DATA.has(id) else "normal"
	return "fairy" if type == "normal" and ability == "pixilate" else type


## Cooldown in seconds: strong moves and those with few PP take longer. A 40-power move
## with 30 PP is back in 1.6 s; a 120-power one with 10 PP takes about 6.5 s. Moves
## without power (status) keep their designed "cd".
static func cooldown(id: String) -> float:
	var d: Dictionary = DATA[id]
	var power: float = d.get("power", 0)
	if power <= 0.0 and d.get("power_by", "") == "":
		return d.get("cd", 0.0)
	if power <= 0.0:
		power = 80.0
	return snappedf(0.6 + 15.0 / maxf(d.get("pp", 15), 1.0) + 3.0 * pow(power / 100.0, 2.0), 0.1)


